        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"model\": \"llama-3.1-8b-instant\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": \"You are a senior Security Operations Center (SOC) analyst. Respond ONLY with a JSON object. \\n\\nFields to include:\\n1. 'relevance_score': A float (1.0 to 10.0) based on how directly the threat affects the provided tech_stack (TECH STACK list: JavaScript, Node.js, Electron, PostgreSQL, Redis, Docker containers, Apache HTTP Server, Ubuntu Linux, OpenSSL, Kubernetes clusters, Terraform infrastructure, AWS IAM, Nginx web servers, Python applications, GitHub Actions CI/CD, Active Directory, Windows Server 2022, IIS, MongoDB databases, Express.js apps, React frameworks, Cisco IOS XE routers, BGP routing infrastructure, Fortinet firewalls).\\n3. 'severity': A single word string (High, Medium, or Low) representing the global danger of the vulnerability.\\n4. 'reasoning': 1 sentence explanation justifying the relevance_score and severity assigned.\\n5. 'matched_tech': An array of strings containing ONLY the specific technologies from the TECH STACK list used to determine the relevance_score. If no matches, return an empty array [].\\n\\nCRITICAL LOGIC:\\n- If the input is nonsensical or noise, set relevance_score to 1.0, severity to 'Low', and summary to 'Noise detected.'\\n- Ahigh 'severity' does not always mean a high 'relevance_score' if the tech_stack does not match.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": {{ JSON.stringify(\"THREAT ARTICLE: \" + $json.fields.input_text + \" | TECH STACK: \" + $json.fields.tech_stack) }}\n    }\n  ],\n  \"response_format\": { \"type\": \"json_object\" }\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
